<title>USA: U.S. factory lard use - Census.</title>
<headline>U.S. factory lard use - Census.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. factories used 39.9 million lbs of lard in edible and inedible product output in May 1997 versus 36.5 million lbs in April and 36.8 million lbs in May 1996 the Census Bureau said.</p>
<p>Usage so far in the 1997 period amounted to 164.4 million lbs versus 185.3 million lbs in the 1996 period.</p>
<p>Usage includes hydrogenated vegetable and animal fats and other fats and oils in process.</p>
</text>
